// brightyard.in services page: 01 Product engineering Products and platforms designed with your users and built
import { link } from '../../../lib/links.mjs';
const site = import.meta.env.SITE_KEY;
---
<div class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="g3 svc">
<div id="svc-eng" class="card rv"><span class="tag">01</span><h3>Product engineering</h3><p>Products and platforms designed with your users and built to be handed over.</p><ul class="ul"><li>Web and mobile applications</li><li>APIs and integrations</li><li>Product design and UX research</li><li>Legacy modernisation in safe slices</li></ul><div class="fit"><b>Good fit if</b>You need a product built or rebuilt and want one team from design to launch.</div><div class="fit"><b>What you get</b>Working software every two weeks, a documented codebase in your repositories, and a team that can stay on after launch.</div></div>
<div id="svc-cloud" class="card rv" style="--d:100ms"><span class="tag">02</span><h3>Cloud and DevOps</h3><p>Infrastructure that scales, deploys often and stays calm on your busiest day.</p><ul class="ul"><li>Cloud migration</li><li>Infrastructure as code</li><li>CI/CD pipelines</li><li>Observability and cost control</li></ul><div class="fit"><b>Good fit if</b>Releases are risky, outages hurt, or the cloud bill keeps surprising you.</div><div class="fit"><b>What you get</b>A pipeline you trust, dashboards you can read, and a written cost and risk report.</div></div>
<div id="svc-data" class="card rv" style="--d:200ms"><span class="tag">03</span><h3>Data and AI</h3><p>From clean data foundations to AI features that hold up with real users.</p><ul class="ul"><li>Data platforms and pipelines</li><li>Dashboards and analytics</li><li>Machine learning and generative AI</li><li>Evaluation, guardrails and AI governance</li></ul><div class="fit"><b>Good fit if</b>An AI pilot impressed in a demo and stalled before production, or nobody trusts the data.</div><div class="fit"><b>What you get</b>A working feature with its evaluation set, monitoring, and a plain-language note on its limits.</div></div>
<div id="svc-a11y" class="card rv"><span class="tag">04</span><h3>Accessibility and quality</h3><p>Find and fix the barriers that stop people using your product, from the team building Xessly.</p><ul class="ul"><li>Accessibility reviews against WCAG</li><li>Remediation in your codebase</li><li>Accessible design systems and components</li><li>Automated and manual testing, including screen readers</li></ul><div class="fit"><b>Good fit if</b>You have an audit, a tender requirement or a customer complaint, or you simply want your product to work for everyone.</div><div class="fit"><b>What you get</b>A prioritised report, fixes in your code and a re-test of every fix. We don't sell overlays and we don't promise compliance; we fix the underlying issues and show you the evidence.</div></div>
<div id="svc-sec" class="card rv" style="--d:100ms"><span class="tag">05</span><h3>Security and support</h3><p>A dependable team behind the systems you run on.</p><ul class="ul"><li>Security reviews and hardening</li><li>Cloud and identity security</li><li>Incident readiness</li><li>24/7 monitoring, service desk and SLAs</li></ul><div class="fit"><b>Good fit if</b>You need someone to keep a live system safe and running, or your current support isn't keeping up.</div><div class="fit"><b>What you get</b>Clear SLAs, a named team, monthly reports and a runbook for every critical system.</div></div>
<a class="card ind rv" style="--d:200ms" href={link('contact', site)}><span class="tag">Not sure yet</span><h3>Start with a conversation</h3><p>Thirty minutes with a senior engineer is enough to point you in the right direction, even if the answer is "not us".</p><span class="btn lime" style="margin-top:22px">Talk to an engineer <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span></a>
</div></div></div>
